{"id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:induced-metric","title":"def:induced-metric","path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.md","line":228,"body":"","kind":"definition","status":"not_started","tex":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex#def:induced-metric","uses":["[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:pullback-immersion-metric]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:riemannian-metric]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","label":"def:induced-metric","line":418,"source":"\\begin{definition}[The metric induced by an immersion]\n\\label{def:induced-metric}\n\n\\uses{lem:pullback-immersion-metric, def:riemannian-metric}\n\n\n\n\n\\dcref{ch2:2.11}\nFor a smooth immersion $F:M\\to(\\widetilde M,\\widetilde g)$ between manifolds with or without boundary, the induced metric is the Riemannian metric $F^*\\widetilde g$. An immersion or embedding with $F^*\\widetilde g=g$ is respectively an isometric immersion or embedding. For a submanifold, the induced metric is the restriction of the ambient metric to tangent vectors.\n\\end{definition}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Definition</div></section>[The metric induced by an immersion] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6465663a696e64756365642d6d6574726963\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Apullback-immersion-metric\">↗ lem:pullback-immersion-metric</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Ariemannian-metric\">↗ def:riemannian-metric</a> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source-references\" role=\"list\" style=\"display:block\"><span class=\"tex-dcref\" role=\"listitem\" style=\"display:block\">1. ch2:2.11</span></span>For a smooth immersion <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$F:M\\to (\\widetilde M,\\widetilde g)$\">$F:M\\to (\\widetilde M,\\widetilde g)$</span> between manifolds with or without boundary, the induced metric is the Riemannian metric <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$F^*\\widetilde g$\">$F^*\\widetilde g$</span>. An immersion or embedding with <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$F^*\\widetilde g=g$\">$F^*\\widetilde g=g$</span> is respectively an isometric immersion or embedding. For a submanifold, the induced metric is the restriction of the ambient metric to tangent vectors. ","warnings":[]},"previous":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:pullback-immersion-metric","next":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#ex:spheres","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:pullback-immersion-metric","title":"lem:pullback-immersion-metric","label":"lem:pullback-immersion-metric"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:riemannian-metric","title":"def:riemannian-metric","label":"def:riemannian-metric"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#ex:spheres","title":"ex:spheres","label":"ex:spheres"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:ambient-tangent-bundle-riemannian","title":"lem:ambient-tangent-bundle-riemannian","label":"lem:ambient-tangent-bundle-riemannian"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#ex:metrics-in-graph-coordinates","title":"ex:metrics-in-graph-coordinates","label":"ex:metrics-in-graph-coordinates"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#ex:surfaces-of-revolution","title":"ex:surfaces-of-revolution","label":"ex:surfaces-of-revolution"}